{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789647573,"nonce":"G9h48fcS41sJXIWxgSbnqp8UTig=","message":"Architecture audit for zypy: crates/zyntax_python/src/main.rs constructs TieredRuntime, not InterpRuntime. Its beadie ladder is native Cranelift tier 0 -\u003e Cranelift tier 1 -\u003e LLVM tier 2 when ZYPY_LLVM=1; ProfileConfig defaults promote at 100 and 1000 calls. Cranelift host_isa fixes opt_level=speed process-wide, and OptimizationTier::cranelift_opt_level is unused, so tier 1 does not gain a stronger Cranelift optimizer. It changes OSR probe/helper mode and recompiles essentially the same body. The separate InterpRuntime has the intended interpreter -\u003e one Cranelift -\u003e LLVM policy, but zypy does not use it. Aligning zypy with that ladder requires integrating its Python snapshot/plugin/collector setup with InterpRuntime, not merely renumbering tiers. Until then the native ladder should avoid a redundant Cranelift recompile when LLVM is selected.","files":null}]}